 following appeal to archetypal structure explains a character's appeal, not that comparative benefit. Earlier arguments for inherited narrative supply relevant background, but do not establish this minimum-divinity claim; no device excludes criticism.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"startEvent\": 2341,\n      \"endEvent\": 2348,\n      \"contextStartEvent\": 2271,\n      \"contextEndEvent\": 2367,\n      \"speaker\": \"A\",\n      \"quote\": \"it maintains its validity across all sets of potential environmental transformations\",\n      \"form\": \"no\",\n      \"substitution\": \"no\",\n      \"protection\": \"unclear\",\n      \"emotionalDevices\": [\"none\"],\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Against environmental mismatch, Peterson asserts that the underlying abstraction survives every potential transformation (E2341–2348). That wording could insulate its relevance from contrary environments. However, E2294–2340 offers an argument from enduring adaptive problems and brain organization, and the claim concerns an abstract landscape rather than every inherited prescription; protective use remains uncertain.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"contrasts\": [\n    {\n      \"startEvent\": 1852,\n      \"endEvent\": 1868,\n      \"speaker\": \"A\",\n      \"quote\": \"sometimes people find a collapse of their faith actually freeing\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Peterson qualifies his preceding claim that abandoning belief leads to nihilism. He accepts successful departures from faith and explicitly declines to dispute the benefit reported by Harris's supporters.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"startEvent\": 2675,\n      \"endEvent\": 2754,\n      \"speaker\": \"B\",\n      \"quote\": \"I'm not saying that you should personally be overwhelmed by the death toll every day\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Harris supports his criticism of selective compassion with a described study and explains the inconsistency when adding another needy child reduces aid. He then limits his prescription to collective decisions rather than demanding unlimited personal distress.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}}
